    //! `t3.dfh.be.hm.za`'s upper reading) on a machine also building for a
    //! sibling lane. Every test sits an order of magnitude inside the 40 s slow
    //! mark and further still inside the 120 s hard kill, so **the binding
    //! split fallback recorded above was not triggered**.
    //!
    //! # Flag-live / no-attempt-count audit (`t3.dfh.be.hm.85`)
    //!
    //! Both cross-cutting constraints are invisible per-lane, so they are
    //! recorded once, here, over the whole Task.
    //!
    //! **The tail flag is LIVE in every fixture.** This module builds its
    //! config in exactly one place — [`lifecycle_fixture`], through
    //! [`tail_enabled_config`], which sets `tail.enabled = true` — and all
    //! three tests consume it. The E2E file's single builder
    //! (`setup_rebase_harness`) sets `opts.tail.enabled = true` and then
    //! ASSERTS the flag reached `harness.config` as a fixture precondition.
    //!
    //! **No assertion in the Task presumes an attempt or retry count.** The
    //! distinction the audit turns on: `observe_checkpoint_stable_cut` adds
    //! exactly `1` to `stable_cut_total{outcome}` per tick DECISION, and a
    //! tick's proven read is one read, so there is no per-read count to
    //! assert. Every stable-cut assertion here reads `stable_cut_total` as a
    //! one-directional `>= 1` on which decision the tick reached. The `checkpoint_lease_total` family appears in
    //! [`lease_diagnostic`]'s failure OUTPUT only and is asserted on nowhere —
    //! deliberately, because a lease-burning re-base ticks `lost` on the healthy
    //! path. No wall-clock comparison is used as an assertion in either file:
    //! the only `Instant` reads are bounded-poll failure deadlines (and the E2E
    //! `poll_until` re-evaluates its predicate once more AFTER the deadline, so
    //! a slow machine loses no verdict).
